{
  "item": "Embedding-model A/B on Axil's own harnesses: bge-small-en-v1.5 (default) vs granite-embedding-small-english-r2 vs gte-modernbert-base, all unprompted",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "status": "complete: dogfood, CLI latency and LongMemEval s20 on the Mac; LongMemEval m5 and s60 on the second machine",
  "raw_outputs": {
    "mac": "benchmarks/results/model-ab-mac/ (per-question dogfood reports, store rebuild reports, LongMemEval reports with .meta/.load/.err, CLI latency, parity oracle, and the scripts that made them)",
    "second_machine": "benchmarks/results/model-ab-pc/ (written by benchmarks/longmemeval/model-ab/run.sh)"
  },
  "scope_note": "The spec's LongMemEval runs each cover one question type: s20 is the first 20 questions of LongMemEval-S, all single-session-user; m5 is the first 5 of LongMemEval-M, all single-session-assistant. s60 (10 questions per type, benchmarks/longmemeval/model-ab/s60-question-ids.json) was added for bge-small and granite so that a default-model recommendation does not rest on one type. Dogfood is 57 questions; one question moves a hit metric by 0.0175, and two plain runs an hour apart have differed by up to 0.03.",
